# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Two reasons this matters:
#   1. `.env` must never be copied into an image layer — a local build would
#      otherwise bake JWT/Mongo/DeepSeek secrets into the image. (Render clones
#      from git, where .env is ignored, but local `docker build` uses the host
#      directory as-is.)
#   2. Host `node_modules` must not overwrite the container's — native modules
#      such as bcrypt are compiled per-platform and a Windows/macOS build would
#      fail at runtime inside Linux.

node_modules
npm-debug.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

uploads
*.log

README.md
database/schema.sql
